{"pr":196,"result":{"status":"fulfilled","value":{"chunk_id":"4c9130","wall_time_seconds":0.60884775,"exit_code":0,"original_token_count":1505,"output":"{\"baseRefOid\":\"525b17ef47d7bec32cbc6da8161bada9a0587479\",\"body\":\"`apply_version_plan` was 447 lines with the same primitives copied through it: opening a canonical manifest five times, the from/to idempotency guard three times, and the git call with its error mapping three times. Several loops also iterated the whole plan only to `continue` past writes another loop owned.\\n\\nManifest writes are now classified once into an ordered list of steps (`write_steps`) and executed by a single `match` (`apply_write_step`), so the per-file order (version bump first, then every dependency rewrite, then exactly one persist) is data rather than control flow. The order of steps is the order the old loops ran: batched manifests, workspace roots, mixed-routing versions, mixed-routing rewrites, platform writes, optional dependencies. `open_canonical`, `write_version_guarded` (the idempotency precondition that makes a retry safe), `run_git_on_paths`, `active_ecosystems` and `refresh_lockfiles` each live once. `apply_version_plan` is 123 lines.\\n\\nNo behavior change. The existing byte-identity tests pass unchanged, along with the poetry and lockfile-precedence tests added in the stacked-under PR; the graph (849) and CLI (420) suites and `just ci` pass with the same 1,882 tests. The public `apply_version_plan` signature is unchanged.\\n\\nStacked on #195. No user-facing change, so no changeset.\",\"commits\":[{\"authoredDate\":\"2026-10-14T02:45:11Z\",\"authors\":[{\"email\":\"gabe@techworx.dev\",\"id\":\"MDQ6VXNlcjExNjc0Nw==\",\"login\":\"castrog\",\"name\":\"Gabe Castro\"}],\"committedDate\":\"2026-10-14T02:57:39Z\",\"messageBody\":\"…executor\\n\\napply_version_plan is 123 lines instead of 447. Manifest writes are ordered once into steps whose per-file order (bump, then rewrites, then one persist) is data, and a single mat