{"pr":195,"result":{"status":"fulfilled","value":{"chunk_id":"f82cb5","wall_time_seconds":0.634860917,"exit_code":0,"original_token_count":2230,"output":"{\"baseRefOid\":\"4f572fbb5f6c6da51503cf259381823acab06dd9\",\"body\":\"Black-box tests for the areas the coverage report showed untested, chosen for features and invariants rather than line counts. One of them found a real bug, fixed here.\\n\\nBug: Cargo dependencies declared under `[target.<cfg>.dependencies]` (and the dev and build variants) were invisible to the graph and never rewritten. A bump left a stale pin that broke `cargo update` (E208), and a dependent reachable only through a target table was never released. The manifest now enumerates and rewrites every dependency table, reporting each (kind, name) once. Both new tests for it fail on the old code. Includes a changeset.\\n\\nNew tests, all through the real binary unless noted:\\n- Release-commit verification: a stale decision, no changeset consumed, no changelog, manifest not in the diff and a wrong manifest version are each rejected with E165 and their own specific reason (6 tests).\\n- `release artifact-manifest`: symlinked, directory and missing assets are refused with no manifest written, unlisted files are ignored, and an intent without artifact slots is rejected (6 tests).\\n- Cascade: exact pins, every Cargo dependency table rewritten with comments and layout preserved, a target-only dependent, an unevaluable pnpm catalog spec reported without cascading, and a stale linked-group member rejected with E108 (5 tests).\\n- Lockfile refresh at the command-runner seam: poetry, and exactly one Python lockfile refreshed in uv, poetry, pdm order (2 tests).\\n- `release` with nothing left to ship is a typed JSON envelope for both the preview and the real run (1 test).\\n\\nNot tested on purpose: the artifact path-escape branch (E222) and the cascade stale linked-group warning cannot be reached through the CLI, because earlier checks reject those inputs 